 vietnam  can tend to be a tool for the government  the all-powerful dr manhattan mirrors  all the unimaginably powerful heroes  like superman  captain adam or silver surfer but  manhattan's ultimate power leads to an  increasing disconnect from the human  condition  thereby questioning the fundamental  humanity of this type of super being  which tacitly leads us to consider what  connects characters like superman to  people like us  and the kind of cold logic and greater  good mentality that characters like  batman so often fall into  also comes into question with ozymandias  squid-based master plan to unite the  world under a common enemy  by killing millions this brings the very  notion of heroism itself into question  pushing us to examine our own moral  concepts of justice and good  gadget-loving detectives obsessive  crusaders the legacy hero  all these archetypes and more are  expertly folded into a handful of  characters  however as we've seen more still treats  them as real people with complex  psychology  none of them are truly good or truly bad  whereas watchmen looks at the entire  genre the dark knight returns hones in  on a single figure batman it imagines a  much older caped crusader who has aged  in real time  eschewing the then unchallenged  convention of unaging comic book heroes  we see the batman robin dynamic in a new  light too with batman characterizing the  series of robins that have served him as  soldiers in this telling the death of  the second robin jason todd was the  biggest factor in batman's decision to  retire  but when he fails to quell as crime  fighting urges and dawns the cape and  cowl again  he is more than willing to take another  impressionable child under his wing  this directly addresses the inherent  irresponsibility of batman in regards to  enlisting children and teenagers into  his hyper-violent war on crime  miller also reappraises the mythic  perpetual struggle between batman and  the joker here the joker has been pretty  much comatose since batman retired  confined to arkham and seemingly  compliant but after batman returns to  gotham the joker too resurfaces to  continue their feud  miller paints their conflict as an  effect of batman's presence  suggesting that maybe it was batman  himself who caused crime to evolve into  super crime  and the stakes to be irreversibly raised  in gotham city miller also features  superman  as a naive ignorant yes man for the  government who wages a climactic battle  against batman  essentially because the president said  so overall watchmen and the dark knight  returns broke  new ground in the development of  superheroes and were heralded for their  self-aware critiques of the genre but as  revolutionary as they were  both books come to somewhat pessimistic  conclusions about superheroes put simply  they're grim grimy and hella cynical  they both feature the governmental  regulation and prohibition of  superheroes for example  suggesting that the natural response to  super beings would be military  application  and they both paint superheroes as  psychologically compromised  driven by neuroses and disorders  unfortunately the comics industry didn't  really get this  after the massive critical and  commercial success of watchmen in the  dark knight returns  everyone tripped over themselves to  mimic the grim dark aesthetic of these  two revolutionary works  but their imitation was only surface  level and led to what is known as the  dark age of comics  suddenly everything had to be dark and  gritty and superheroes turned into  holes who killed villains  indiscriminately optimism was seen to be  cheesy replaced with baseless angst  blood  gore and rampant over sexualization was  everywhere  but seemingly just for the aesthetic  without the nuance and complexity of  watchmen and the dark knight returns  the stories were ultimately hollow enter  zack snyder  before the dceu snyder was becoming  known as the comic book guy in hollywood  mostly due to his faithful adaptation of  watchmen and during the press for  watchmen snyder lauded two comics over  all  others watchmen duh and the dark knight  returns  even mentioning his desire to adapt the  latter for film  and here's where we get into the real  meat as to why the dceu fell flat on its  face  the same cynical deconstruction that  worked for watchmen and the dark knight  returns  seemed to inform every decision snyder  made when building the dceu  he could only see the superheroes and  the world they inhabit through a grimy  pessimistic lens  but just like the dark age of comics  snyder seemed preoccupied with the dark  surface  rather than the intellectual core  furthering this his overriding warship  of those fabled deconstructivist comics  caused big problems when he drew from  other  less gritty source material to highlight  this let's look at man of steel the  origin story for the granddaddy of all  superheroes  snyder actually draws from a lot of  influences here predominantly the  classic optimistic superman comics  birthright by mark wade and all star  superman by grant morrison the movie  wears these influences on its sleeve  things like clark flying alongside a  herd of zebra and the s crest on his  costume standing for hope that's what  this symbol means  symbol of the house of earl means hope  are pulled straight from birthright he  even lifts this speech almost word for  word from all-star superman you will  give the people of earth  an ideal to strive towards  they will race behind you they will  stumble  they will fall but in time  they will join you in the sun cow but  standards nods to these inspirations are  essentially lip service we get  acknowledgments by the way of shared  design  imagery and dialogue it's not an s  on my world it means hope but snyder  seemingly can't reconcile their hopeful  uplifting themes with his own cynicism  we know this because whenever possible  man of steel takes the dark and gritty  option we covered this 