man returns  from the dead  proving to be the only one who can stop  them and be worthy of the title of  superman thematically the whole story  revolves around the notion that a dark  and gritty superman isn't superman at  all the methods of the four replacement  superman  actually reflect the edgy grim heroes of  the 90s however the only thing snyder  takes away from this  is superman plus death rather than  seeing how superman's death could  fulfill his arc of redeeming him  snyder ignores everything else to once  again hyper focus  on the surface fact that superman done  died  by the time justice league rolled around  the damage had already been done  we pick up where snyder left off  superman's dead  batman's guilt written and struggling  with his violent tendencies and wonder  woman's oddly detached from  everything while we may never know the  entirety of snyder's plans what we do  know paints a somewhat conflicted  picture  on the one hand snyder's vision would  have revealed martian manhunter and  green  lantern completing the iconic justice  league lineup facing off against  darkseid which makes it hard not to pine  for what could have been  but on the other hand even more time  would have been spent in the nightmare  future  with a decimated justice league fighting  back against a brainwashed  fascist superman that part would have  been inspired by tom taylor and brian  buchelado's injustice comics  a grim gritty and cynical deconstructive  tale that asks  what if superman broke bad based on  snyder's previous adaptations it's not  hard to extrapolate  we suspect the same kind of surface  level cynical interpretation would have  come into effect here too  but ultimately we can't know for sure  because snyder didn't get to complete  his vision  and we'll never really know if his  controversial choices would have paid  off  still the fact remains that we did get  most of the story and most of us hated  it  so much so that it killed the idea of an  interconnected cinematic universe  dead it's not all doom and gloom though  dc and warner brothers have stepped back  from their sprawling plans of  connectivity  handing the reins over to a creative  team that are willing to embrace the  bright  playful and hopeful nature of the genre  wonder woman aquaman and shazam  have generated warmer reception from  fans and critics alike  and indicate a less depressing future  for dc films  but what do you think wisecrack did  snyder miss the point  or are we being too hard on the guy let  us know what you think in the comments  thanks to our dope patrons for  supporting the channel and our podcasts  slam that subscribe button and as always  thanks for watching guys  peace  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you

